ngs perhaps are that  the near next annoyed Amanda clock rate  affected foraging performance of workers  so the ones that the colonies that were  treated with that pesticide actually  more forages but those forages were much  less effective at bringing back pollen  which is a limiting factor for colony  growth it's certainly concerning that  having these combination of pesticides  outside could be causing such a severe  impact but we know we've only looked at  two pesticides yeah we know that there  are hundreds of pesticides used out  there millions of areas of agricultural  land are being sprayed with these  pesticides and these bees are being  exposed to them currently pesticides are  actually regulated very tightly but the  focus is very much on what are the  lethal effects so what dosages will kill  bees and particularly honeybees are the  focus of those tests what I think our  study shows is that longer term effects  of lower doses can also be important so  they may be relatively subtle effects on  behavior but their effects on the  individual bees which filter up to the  colony level and can have effects on  whether colonies actually thrive or even  fail you do get a personal feel with  them and especially when you're seeing  them get affected so badly by these  pesticides you're thinking what really  is going on in the world and and you  know are they really being affected this  badly for me it is vital I mean these  are fascinating creatures they're  massively important in the ecosystem so  we can't lose them  you
 

